# XSH dirfd()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.dirfd.001
anchor     functions/dirfd.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       dirfd() of a stream from opendir("d") returns a descriptor that
           fstat() shows to be d, returns the same descriptor again, and
           that descriptor is the stream's own: closedir() closes it.
test       t/001-dirfd.c
